{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, it wouldn't be technology or money or even ending one specific problem.\n\nIt would be this: **I'd make everyone truly *feel* what other people feel.**\n\nNot just understand it intellectually, but viscerally feel it for like, 10 seconds before they act or judge. True, automatic empathy.\n\nI think almost every big problem we have comes from a feeling of separation \u2014 like \"me vs. you,\" \"us vs. them.\" Greed, hate, cruelty, wars, even just being mean to someone online... it all happens when we can't really feel the impact we have on another person.\n\nIf empathy was our default setting:\n\n* No one could ignore hunger or homelessness, because you'd feel it like it was your own.\n* No one would want war, because you'd feel the grief on both sides.\n* People wouldn't stay in hate, because you'd feel how heavy and lonely it is to be the person you hate.\n* And on the flip side, kindness would be contagious too. You'd feel the joy you gave someone else.\n\nI wouldn't want to make the world perfect or remove all struggle - struggle is how we grow, how we find meaning and resilience. But I would want to remove the *loneliness* of struggle. No one would ever feel completely unseen or alone in what they're going through.\n\nWe'd still disagree. We'd still be wildly different. But we'd disagree like family, not like strangers.\n\nWhat about you? If you had that one change - what would you pick?",
